                           one writes, through the guards `read` and `write` answer (sync.z), one copy
                           per value type; both classes are this template, @@P0@@ their one type. The lock and the value live in a heap block every handle shares, as a
                           Mutex's do. A ReadGuard and a WriteGuard are `{z_rwlock_t* l; T* value}`
                           (templates ReadGuard, WriteGuard): `read` and `write` fill one. */
                        typedef struct z_@@NAME@@_blk {
                            z_rwlock_t l;
                            Z_ATOMIC(uint64_t) refs;
                            @@P0@@ value;
                        } z_@@NAME@@_blk;

                        typedef struct z_@@NAME@@_t {
                            z_@@NAME@@_blk* b;
                        } z_@@NAME@@_t;

                        """
                )
